Using $\size {\max_a f_a - \max_a g_a} \le \max_a \size {f_a - g_a}$:
{{begin-eqn}}
{{eqn | l = \norm {\TT V - \TT W}_\infty
| o = \le
| r = \gamma \max_{s, a} \sum_{s'} \map P {s' \mid s, a} \size {\map V {s'} - \map W {s'} }
}}
{{eqn | o = \le
| r = \gamma \norm {V - W}_\infty
}}
{{end-eqn}}
So $\TT$ is a [[Definition:Contraction Mapping|contraction]] with modulus $\gamma$.

Iterating $\TT$ is [[Definition:Value Iteration|value iteration]], and:
:$\norm {\TT^n V - V^*}_\infty \le \gamma^n \norm {V - V^*}_\infty$
{{qed}}
